netlink: take RTM_SETLINK as Linux's rtnl_setlink() does

What: RTM_SETLINK changes an existing interface and nothing else: it ignores
NLM_F_CREATE, NLM_F_EXCL and NLM_F_REPLACE, which only RTM_NEWLINK takes, as
net/core/rtnetlink.c:rtnl_setlink() does. A request that names neither an
index nor an interface name fails with EINVAL and one whose name no
interface has with ENODEV, as in Linux; before, the first failed with EINVAL
whenever NLM_F_CREATE was set, and with EEXIST on an existing interface when
NLM_F_EXCL was. Under hostinet, whose RTM_SETLINK changes nothing, these flags
no longer fail either.

Why: netavark brings each link up with RTM_SETLINK and the flags
NLM_F_ACK|NLM_F_EXCL|NLM_F_CREATE (src/network/netlink.rs, set_up(), in
1.4.0, 1.14.0 and 1.17.2). Every Podman container on a netavark network
failed at its first request, the loopback interface of its namespace:
"netavark: Netlink error: Invalid argument (os error 22)".

Upstream: none found (gVisor master of 2026-11-17 still fails such a request
with EINVAL); drop this patch when upstream takes these flags as Linux does.

Verified:
- The new syscall test NetlinkRouteTest.SetLinkIgnoresNewLinkFlags, built in
  gVisor's builder container and run as root with CAP_NET_ADMIN, CAP_NET_RAW
  and CAP_SYS_ADMIN, passes on Linux 7.0 under runc and on runsc with this
  patch, under the runtime arguments of runsc and of runsc-nested, and fails
  on ALE's 0.1.2. The whole socket_netlink_route_test passes on runsc (126
  tests with patches 0011 to 0014), as do
  //pkg/sentry/socket/netlink/route:route_test and
  //pkg/sentry/socket/netstack:netstack_test.
- netavark 1.4.0 (Podman 4.9.3, Ubuntu 24.04), 1.14.0 (Podman 5.4.2, Debian
  13) and 1.17.2 (Podman 5.8.9, Fedora 43) in sandboxes under runsc-nested
  brought the container's loopback interface up; the next failure was
  netavark's lookup of the host end of the veth (patch 0013).

diff --git a/pkg/sentry/socket/hostinet/stack.go b/pkg/sentry/socket/hostinet/stack.go
index 1e31fa2..ad937f1 100644
--- a/pkg/sentry/socket/hostinet/stack.go
+++ b/pkg/sentry/socket/hostinet/stack.go
@@ -288,8 +288,9 @@ func (s *Stack) SetInterface(ctx context.Context, msg *nlmsg.Message) *syserr.Er
 		return syserr.ErrNoDevice
 	}
 
-	flags := msg.Header().Flags
-	if flags&(linux.NLM_F_EXCL|linux.NLM_F_REPLACE) != 0 {
+	// Linux's rtnl_setlink ignores NLM_F_EXCL and NLM_F_REPLACE, which only
+	// RTM_NEWLINK takes.
+	if hdr := msg.Header(); hdr.Type != linux.RTM_SETLINK && hdr.Flags&(linux.NLM_F_EXCL|linux.NLM_F_REPLACE) != 0 {
 		return syserr.ErrExists
 	}
 
